# Keep internal working files OFF the public deployment.
#
# Why this file exists (2026-09-04): every one of these paths was fetchable with a
# plain GET on the review URL. Verified by curl, all HTTP 200:
#
#   /CLIENT-BRIEF.md            the brief, including voice notes, the "never mention
#                               Medicaid" rule, and the competitor positioning
#   /BUILD-NOTES.md             56KB of build and audit history
#   /build/reviews_data.py      the review set AND the full exclusion list of every
#                               non-five-star review deliberately left off the site
#   /build/GHL-WIRING.md        the lead-routing cutover checklist
#   /build/common.py            generator source, including the lead wiring config
#   /build/COPY-DECK-2026-09-04.md   client-reviewer rulings and the reasoning behind them
#
# The reviews exclusion list is the worst of those: it is a public, machine-readable
# record that negative reviews were curated out. Nothing here is meant for anyone
# outside the agency, and the review URL is about to be sent to the client.
#
# Vercel serves this repo as a static tree, so anything committed and not ignored is
# public. There is no build step on Vercel: the generators run locally and commit
# their output, which is why excluding build/ cannot break the deployment.
#
# Rule of thumb: only pages, assets and robots.txt belong on the deployment. If you add
# a new working file, add it here in the same commit.

# Build system. Runs locally only; never needed at serve time.
build/

# Internal documentation.
*.md

# Local tooling and scratch.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
node_modules/
